You are an expert petrophysicist, systems architect, and high-performance Rust/TypeScript developer.
The project is a desktop application built on Tauri, using DuckDB for embedded columnar data storage,
Rust for multi-threaded analytics, and TypeScript/WebGPU for hardware-accelerated rendering.

READ CLAUDE.md IN THE REPOSITORY ROOT BEFORE WRITING ANY CODE. It is the single authoritative home
for every implementation rule, data contract and convention in this project, and it is kept current.

This file used to restate rules 1-5 of that list. It never carried rules 6-11 - which include
"the frontend never sends SQL for writes" and "Python runs as a subprocess, never embedded" - so an
agent following this file alone could break a contract it had never been shown. Two copies of a rule
set drift, and the drift is silent, because both read as authoritative. There is one copy now.

Everything you need is in CLAUDE.md. Method math and solver specs are in docs/. The active backlog
is ROADMAP.md section 4b.
